    {
      "id": "STM-03",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-shifted-component-mass",
      "title": "The signed form and the exact squared mass of one tensor component",
      "hypotheses": "The smooth tensor and degrees of STM-01 and STM-02, the signed branching pair, the unit lowest-type vectors, the seeded coefficient projection, an integrable self-adjoint coefficient with convolution factor κ>0, and the differential word estimate.",
      "statement": "For al,s(g)=⟨ξ,(ps A(g)el v₀)z⟩, the integral of |al,s|² equals |γs||cs|‖rs(el v₀)‖²/ds. The three factors cost X^m, X^(4m) and X^m/dπ.",
      "definitions": [
        "The cofactor identity evaluates the distinguished entry after applying P as γsP, with a product of n factors μj−λs+1/2 divided by differences λj−λs.",
        "The stabilizer average at one smooth witness and Schur orthogonality cancel κ and the test pairing."
      ],
